  "configuration_id": "config_028",
  "reason": "The current best is config_018 (multimodal, multiprofile, scvi_n200 + resnet50, transformer, concat; acc=0.688), which shows that transformer aggregation with multimodal fusion substantially outperforms avgpool (0.632) and RNA-only transformer (0.653). In the singleprofile setting, resnet50 and imagenet_vit_l performed nearly identically (0.536 vs 0.532), but that context lacked multiprofile aggregation. With transformer aggregation, the image features interact with multiple RNA profiles, so a more expressive image encoder (ViT-L) could capture richer spatial features that complement the RNA representations. config_028 is a clean single-variable change from config_018 (only image encoder: resnet50 → imagenet_vit_l), isolating the effect of image representation quality in the best-performing configuration. If it improves, it signals that image encoder capacity is a key lever; if not, it confirms resnet50 suffices and redirects attention to RNA encoder or fusion choices. This is the highest-information next step under the limited budget."
}

